    "description": "UAMD-2: Laffs\n\nUndectectable Additive Manufactured Dagger. Second model.\n\nA angled spine 3DP dagger with a wide, tanto styled blade tip. Simple to print and use. Melt it down after use.\n\n20mm longer than the UAMD-1; has a 24mm wide blade for a wider wound cavity. Due to a wider blade, this design is more for stomach/under the ribcage \nuse, unlike Model 1's more slender blade for getting between ribs. Tradeoff simply being Model 2 should be more durable and less chance of bending.\n\n\n\nPrinter Used: Ender 3 V2\n\nFilament Used: PLA+ (More durable if printed in CF Nylon, though melting it down after use would be a bit more difficult.)\n\nPrint Settings:\n\nExtruder: 220C \nBed: 56C \nFirst Layer Print Height: .2mm \nStandard Layer Height: .12mm\nWall Thickness: .40 \nWall Perimeters: 8+\nInfill: 50%+\n\n\n\nNote: Yes, ik, its small. (165mm) That be the idea you dorks >.> ",
